FerrionOS change to upstream RedoxFS (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 5ba45a6887374ab425326656a276bb3b62eba7dc after the existing recipe patches. Found by the deterministic simulation in sim/redoxfs (sim/redoxfs/run.sh replay FILE runs a replay).

link_node built a directory entry from any name, and a name longer than 252 bytes panicked in DirEntry::new, stopping the whole file system service. It now returns EINVAL for names a directory entry cannot hold.

Replay: link to a 253-byte name panics at src/dir.rs:19. Without this patch 18 of 120 simulated seeds fail.
diff --git a/src/transaction.rs b/src/transaction.rs
index 3cdf6fa..3796fe5 100644
--- a/src/transaction.rs
+++ b/src/transaction.rs
@@ -898,6 +898,9 @@ impl<'a, D: Disk> Transaction<'a, D> {
         name: &str,
         node_ptr: TreePtr<Node>,
     ) -> Result<()> {
+        if name.is_empty() || name.contains(':') || name.len() > DIR_ENTRY_MAX_LENGTH {
+            return Err(Error::new(EINVAL));
+        }
         let mut parent = self.read_tree(parent_ptr)?;
         let mut node = self.read_tree(node_ptr)?;
 
